</ul><h1>Nothing Special</h1><p>There are a lot of times when being a good friend means being there for someone and putting in real work to help them out of a bad situation. Sleepless nights, long days, tough conversations. There are times, in other words, when being a good friend can be difficult, physically and emotionally.</p>
<p>But then there are those other times when really all you need to do is act vaguely stable. You know, those stretches where every other person or thing in your friend’s life is malfunctioning, and you get brownie points just for being normal and not adding to the shitstorm.</p>
<p>That’s us today.</p>
<p>It’s Black Friday, a day of consumerist chaos.</p>
<p>And that’s crazy, isn’t it? Because it comes after a day of nutritional excess and/or familial tensions. Which itself comes after a day of either marathon cleaning and meal prep, or many grueling hours of travel that would be stressful even without the potential for plans being disrupted by bad weather, system outages, or A HUGE PLUME OF LITERAL FUCKING LEAD IN THE AIR.</p>
<p>(Or maybe that wasn’t an issue on Wednesday? At the time of writing this, it’s unclear whether the detonation will happen or not. But still, there was a chance that, at one point, a giant cloud of lead had been a part of your travel considerations. And that’s WILD.)</p>
<p>Later today or later this weekend, you may have to repeat this treacherous travel in the reverse direction, or else put your house back together after hosting, and then get immediately into the festive spirit.</p>
<p>And so, while you still haven’t recovered from the holiday, and you’re being told that you need to get the big items on everyone’s list TODAY or risk losing out on AMAZING SAVINGS, and you can see your neighbors hanging lights from their gutters while yours remain stashed away in the basement, still tangled from last year… we’re just over here, cool as cucumbers, offering something super basic: a charging phone mount for your car.</p>
<p>Not a very flashy item, is what we’re saying. Because there’s plenty of flash everywhere else today.</p>
<p>Now, we would be remiss not to say, despite its lack of sex appeal, this is a good mount. <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0CVXL1CL9?plpRedirect=mhFallback&ref=clp_hp_h_pc&tag=mehdown-20#averageCustomerReviewsAnchor">Like, 4.3-out-of-5-on-Amazon good</a> (albeit with a different brand name, but it is the same product).</p>
<p>User Dbrozov lays out some good reasons for the high marks:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I’ve tried several vent mounts now and they all have the same issue where they sag under the weight of a phone or the magnets are weak. Well, MagSafe is strong for starters so I have yet to have my phone fall or shake loose which was immediately a 5 star in my book. The mount itself doesn’t shake because of the extra clasp and threaded tightening ring to make it tight and secure.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Wow, so it’s entirely reliable, easy to deal with, and refreshingly bland.</p>
<p>Just like us today.</p>
<p>Stay sane out there, friends.</p>